-# DJ independent prototype — Issue1064
+# Manual DJ prototype — Issue1064
 
-Entry: `remake/previews/dj/index.html` over the existing HTTP preview server. No build, package install, audio/image downloads or game SAVE required. From the repo root, an existing Python runtime can serve it with `python3 -m http.server 8123 --bind 127.0.0.1`; then use `http://127.0.0.1:8123/remake/previews/dj/`. A task-local candidate bundle can use the same server command with `--directory candidate`. A server/browser was not launched by this task around the recorded local Chrome refusal.
+Entry: `remake/previews/dj/index.html`, using the existing permitted HTTP preview/normal PR CI environment. Buildless; no dependency installation, external media or game SAVE required. This revision did not launch a local server/browser or change a recorded browser restriction.
 
-Press 音を開始. The initial level is 18%; mute and volume are available. With assistance ON, the fixed pair is tempo/phrase-aligned when a transfer is reserved. At the next 8-bar boundary, move the horizontal fader to the other deck over 8 bars. The next transfer is queued automatically. Missing the endpoint has no score, penalty or resource effect. Optional J/tap feedback is disabled during transfers.
+1. Prepare audio (initial volume 18%). Preparation alone starts neither deck. Mute/volume are available before playback.
+2. Manually match PITCH/BPM: the fixed test pair starts at A128/B126. Press PLAY A, then press the separate large PLAY B at the displayed phrase head yourself. There is no SYNC, automatic tempo blending, scheduled PLAY, automatic seek or automatic fader movement. PLAY uses the audio clock when its user request is accepted; it does not quantize to the guide.
+3. Use the upper A/lower B actual-PCM waveforms and ±1/16-beat nudges to align phase. Both use the same seven-second scale/current line. Nudging seeks the playing audio; stopped-deck nudge is disabled. The B half-beat button is a labelled test control.
+4. Move the horizontal crossfader over the indicated eight bars. It changes equal-power gains only. There is no EQ/CUE, tapping mini-game, scoring or pass/fail. Fader percentages show position, not linear gain.
 
-For manual work, turn reservation assistance OFF. Change tempo separately from ±1/16-beat nudges. Bを半拍ずらして試す introduces an actual half-beat seek; A/B synchronization aligns both tempo and the full 32-beat phrase. Rate changes also change pitch; key lock is not implemented. B's bass is pretransposed to match A under assisted 128 BPM. Waveforms above the decks are actual generated PCM peaks on a common seven-second scale, A above B, with a shared playhead. The % readout is fader position, not linear gain; the audio uses equal-power gains with short ramps.
+Remaining bars, the last four beats and NEXT HEAD are provisional visual entry guidance, not an input tolerance or reservation mechanism. Missing a head never starts a stopped deck. Initial PLAY begins at beat zero; per-deck PAUSE/PLAY preserves its head. A subsequent transfer requires the player to stop/start or time the other deck; there is no CUE/reset-to-head feature. Beat-phase and 32-beat phrase offset are separately displayed; matching beats alone does not repair a whole-bar error. This remains a fixed-pair prototype rather than a finished set-management interface.
 
-Both mono test tracks are original procedural sound (kick/hat/snare/bass), 32 beats each, nominal 128/126 BPM. Buffer duration rounding is included in the actual playback-rate calculation. No finished EDM, stock audio, sampled song, third-party sprites or product UI images are included. RED ROOM is a prototype label, not an adopted story venue. Pixel graphics are original code placeholders, not approved character art.
+Both mono tracks are original procedural test sound (kick/hat/snare/bass), 32 beats each. Buffer rounding is included in the actual playback-rate calculation. B's existing bass is pretransposed for manually matching 128 BPM; there is no key lock and pitch follows tempo. No finished EDM, recorded songs, third-party samples, sprites or product interface images are included.
 
-All transport/phase calculations use AudioContext time, not animation frame counts. A/B sources keep their own anchors. The louder side chooses the visual beat master with 40/60% hysteresis; the reserved outgoing deck times the 8-bar interval. VJ brightness uses the mixed-output analyser; the dancer's alternating steps use the visual master's actual beat. Reduced motion keeps a static pose and restrained VJ. No VJ scoring/input.
+AudioContext time drives playback, waveforms and beat positions. A/B keep independent anchors and rates. The active/louder deck chooses the visual beat master with 40/60% hysteresis. The outgoing guide deck measures the eight-bar window, but never modifies audio. The VJ uses mixed-output RMS. A small passive window below the controls shows a four-beat original code dancer and, separately, a short geometric glamorous-character proposal. These are labelled placeholders, not adopted character art. Reduced motion uses static background VJ; no flashing or overlay over PLAY/waveforms.
 
-Pause, hidden tabs and audio interruption stop voices; return requires a user start. Seeking crossfades old/new voices for 8ms and releases the old nodes. Page exit disconnects/closes the graph; bfcache navigation pauses for manual resume. No localStorage/sessionStorage, game state import, economy, day/time or save-schema changes.
+Pause, hidden tabs and audio interruption stop/disconnect voices. Whole-transport resume restores only previously playing decks, without pitch matching. Individual pause preserves its position. Seek ramps old/new sources over 8ms and releases old nodes. Page exit disconnects/closes the graph; bfcache navigation pauses. No localStorage/sessionStorage, game-state import, economy, time or SAVE-schema changes.
 
